{% comment %}
  URL map + live preview image for the dispenser custom color picker.
  Rendered by product-custom-colors.liquid inside its root element.
  One entry per Primary__Secondary combination; assets are cc-<P>__<S>.webp,
  rendered by content/pipeline/colourway/cw_custom.py in the Studio vault.
  Keys use the display color names; values are versioned asset URLs.
{% endcomment %}

<div class="product-custom-colors__preview" data-custom-preview hidden>
  <model-viewer
    id="CustomColorModel-{{ section.id }}"
    {%- comment -%}
      dispenser-custom-ao.glb carries a baked ambient occlusion map on the
      Primary and Secondary materials. The previous dispenser-custom.glb is kept
      in assets as an instant revert; swapping this one line back also requires
      reverting the albedo tables, since AO darkens the sampled band and the
      tables were re-solved against it. Built by
      pipeline/colourway/glb_export_ao.py in the Studio vault.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    data-glb-src="{{ 'dispenser-custom-ao.glb' | asset_url }}"
    alt="Interactive preview of the dispenser in the selected custom colors"
    camera-controls
    touch-action="pan-y"
    interaction-prompt="auto"
    {%- comment -%}
      Rendering config is CALIBRATED, not decorative. tone-mapping, exposure and
      the data-albedo table in product-custom-colors.liquid are ONE MATCHED SET
      and must be changed together. Measured on 2026-08-18, full method and
      delta tables in Studio vault: projects/shopify/content/viewer-cal-REPORT.md

      Why not neutral: the Khronos PBR Neutral curve desaturates bright
      saturated colors by mixing them toward white, which raises the blue
      channel of Yellow and Orange by 43 to 63 points no matter what albedo is
      supplied (with blue albedo at zero, blue still rendered 54). That lift is
      channel coupled, so no per color albedo can invert it.

      Why linear and not cineon (round 2, 2026-08-18): cineon has no coupling
      and hit the color target, but its shoulder flattened the model. At a
      matched white brightness the hopper and funnel showed a luminance band
      spread of 8.5 of 255 under cineon versus 47 under neutral and 87 under
      linear, which is why the part read as a flat silhouette. Linear has a
      constant slope, so it preserves the geometry's own shading, and it still
      has zero channel coupling. Its only cost is highlight clipping, which is
      held near 10 percent of part pixels by a per channel albedo ceiling baked
      into the tables. Exposure is low because the specular floor scales with
      it, and the floor is what sets the error on Black and on zero channels.
      Round 3 (2026-08-18) added baked ambient occlusion to the GLB and raised
      shadow-intensity from 2 to 2.5 (mean ground shadow alpha 119.3 to 143.3 of
      255; 3.0 was rejected at 157.2). The AO map is now part of the matched set:
      it darkens the sampled band, so the albedo tables were re-solved against it
      and are not interchangeable with the pre AO ones.
      Round 4 (2026-08-18) rebuilt the mesh: smooth normals by angle plus per
      object decimate ratios, so exposure moved 0.17 to 0.15 and both albedo
      tables were re-solved. Geometry, AO map, tone mapping, exposure and the
      tables are all one matched set.
      Upgrading assets/model-viewer.min.js requires re-running the calibration.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    tone-mapping="linear"
    exposure="0.15"
    shadow-intensity="2.5"
    shadow-softness="0.8"
    camera-orbit="200deg 78deg auto"
    style="width: 100%; height: 100%;"
  ></model-viewer>
  <img
    id="CustomColorPreview-{{ section.id }}"
    alt="Preview of the dispenser in the selected custom colors"
    loading="lazy"
    width="620"
    height="1119"
    hidden
  >
  <p class="caption product-custom-colors__preview-chip">Custom color preview, drag to rotate</p>
  <p class="caption product-custom-colors__preview-note">3D preview is simplified for fast loading. The product you receive is printed smooth and precise.</p>
</div>

<script type="module" src="{{ 'model-viewer.min.js' | asset_url }}"></script>

